hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20867","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Asim, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, from one who was the riding companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was his companion on a donkey, and the donkey stumbled, so I said: Perish Satan, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Do not say: Perish Satan, for when you say: Perish Satan, Satan becomes great in himself and says: I threw him down with my strength, but when you say: In the name of Allah, he shrinks before it until he becomes smaller than a fly."
"20868","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim, he said: I heard Abu Tamimah narrating from the riding companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Shu'bah said: Asim said: From Abu Tamimah, from a man, from the riding companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The donkey stumbled with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I said: Perish Satan, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say: Perish Satan, for when you say: Perish Satan, he becomes great and says: With my strength I threw him down, and when you say: In the name of Allah, he shrinks until he becomes like the fly."
